  "origin": "magpie-ai-case-study",
  "operation": "prepare",
  "summary": "Dev lifecycle 7.10.0 -> 7.19.0 (dev canonical skill 2.8.0 -> 2.16.0). 2.9.0/7.11.0: Plan Step 4 rework requires developer sign-off on the diff (not just a re-audit 'go') before finalization. 2.9.0-2.11.0/7.11.0-7.13.0: Context Gathering Step 3.6 identifies the HLD container(s) in scope for the sign-off summary; Plan Step 5 adds a second, distinct sign-off on the persisted 1-plan.md (via patterns/write-confirm.md) separate from Step 3's draft approval; Plan Step 6 makes committing 1-plan.md a manual developer-run operation, matching Ceremony's checkout. 2.12.0/7.14.0: Implement Step 3 closes the gap where self-run verification was treated as implicit sign-off -- verification is a developer confirmation gate, not something self-certified because a command exited 0 in the agent's sandbox; a delegated worker lacking a tool is never grounds for the orchestrator to take the gate over. 2.13.0/7.15.0: patterns/satellite-review.md adds an explicit 'Handoff -- present and approve' step (worker -> orchestrator -> developer; a satellite go verdict is an input to the sign-off gate, never a substitute). 2.14.0/7.16.0: stat.json tracks author (git config user.name), set once at init. 2.15.0/7.17.0: derived, non-hand-set Flags column/field (retried/rework/scope_change/reopened/failed_check) on stage/step metrics, kept optional in the schema so it never breaks validation of pre-existing stat.json documents. 7.18.0: Documentation Principles' length budget counts prose only -- diagrams and tables are exempt -- and splitting a companion doc is reframed as a normal move, not a last resort. 7.19.0: independent consistency review (reading every touched file plus its untouched neighbors) found and fixed leftover 7.5.0 'softening' language that contradicted the restored gates -- patterns/approvals.md and patterns/do-report-commit.md no longer license continuing past a gated commit; patterns/write-confirm.md gets an explicit exception for when a call site names it as a sign-off gate; INTENT.md's verify checklist no longer tells a future installer to remove the fixed sign-off gates or allow a local-draft Plan Mode fallback; Implement's never-commit-yourself rule is narrowed to git add/git commit specifically (not git mv, used by Document's local archival) and Document's own commit line now states the same never-commit rule explicitly; every stage's shared boilerplate now names the fixed sign-off gates as an explicit exception instead of relying on a cross-reference; author was made optional in the schema to match flags, for the same stated compatibility reason; templates/report.md's table skeletons and patterns/announce-progress.md and patterns/metrics.md's stale references were brought in sync. All 22 timing.test.mjs cases pass; stat.schema.json remains valid JSON.",
  "package_version": "7.19.0",
